  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISF: OPTs-Israel: Support to Violence Reduction and Political Settlement Negotiations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Against the backdrop of continued uncertainty, instability and a deepening humanitarian crisis, the Negotiations Support Programme (NSP) aims to support the negotiating capacity of the PLO and PA and the achievement of Palestinian political coherence to contribute to the overall goal of a two-state solution. The theory of change elucidates that if the relevant institutions (including Office of the President of the PLO and the Negotiations Affairs Department) are provided with technical and material support to develop negotiating objectives and agendas; and if intra-Palestinian dialogue helps to establish a more coherent approach to negotiations, then Palestinian positions will be clearer, better articulated and better represented in ongoing and future interactions with GoI. This will have a ripple effect for potential future negotiations which will be enhanced through timely, well developed, and politically supported positions on key topics with a higher chance of a positive outcome.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The programme aims to support Palestinian negotiating capacity and the 
achievement of Palestinian political coherence on negotiating issues to contribute 
to the overall goal of a two-state solution. The programme has two workstreams: 
an institutional support workstream under which draw-down technical advice and 
material support is provided to negotiating institutions and an intra-Palestinian 
workstream, which supports initiatives that seek to build coherence around key 
conflict settlement issues.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
